data: {"ThreadDataMiddleware.before_agent": {"thread_data": {"workspace_path": "/home/nan/c_project/deer-flow/backend/.deer-flow/users/4daeaa31-7ac6-4eb5-bdf6-8029abc51fab/threads/1aa43d59-cfdb-4cd9-a88a-3585086bd6fb/user-data/workspace", "uploads_path": "/home/nan/c_project/deer-flow/backend/.deer-flow/users/4daeaa31-7ac6-4eb5-bdf6-8029abc51fab/threads/1aa43d59-cfdb-4cd9-a88a-3585086bd6fb/user-data/uploads", "outputs_path": "/home/nan/c_project/deer-flow/backend/.deer-flow/users/4daeaa31-7ac6-4eb5-bdf6-8029abc51fab/threads/1aa43d59-cfdb-4cd9-a88a-3585086bd6fb/user-data/outputs"}, "messages": [{"content": "<system-reminder>\n<memory>\nUser Context:\n- Personal: User prefers to communicate in 中文 (Chinese) for agent design conversations. User is engaged in building custom AI agents and working with system configuration tools like SOUL.md. Technical interests include agent personality design and system prompt engineering. User also plans family travel, specifically with young children (6-year-old), and values detailed, constraint-aware planning with structured deliverables.\n- Current Focus: User has pivoted away from the \"aaaaaa\" agent design project and is now requesting a completely different task: a 7-day Tokyo family travel itinerary for 2 adults and a 6-year-old child, staying near Shinjuku Station. The request was highly structured with 7 explicit constraints including daily activity limits, meal requirements, rainy day contingencies, and a specific Markdown output format. User also specified a phased work approach: clarify goals first, then progress in stages rather than delivering a complete answer immediately. The assistant completed all 5 phases (information gathering, regional clustering, framework building, detail supplementation, and final Markdown output) and delivered a comprehensive itinerary with regional clustering to minimize transfers, fatigue-aware pacing for a 6-year-old, and advance booking warnings for Ghibli Museum and teamLab Planets. User's pattern of providing detailed constraints and expecting structured, multi-phase deliverables is evident. The \"aaaaaa\" agent project appears abandoned or on hold.\n\nHistory:\n- Recent: User has been actively engaged in custom AI agent development, working with a system that supports SOUL.md configuration files for agent personality and behavior definition. Recent activities include initiating agent creation workflows, specifying agent purposes (starting with a general request then narrowing to 简历编辑/resume editing for an agent named \"test\"), and participating in personalization workflows to tailor agent design. There was a naming confusion where assistant assumed the agent was called \"test1\" but user clarified they wanted the original \"test\" agent. However, user then pivoted to a completely new agent named \"aaaaaa\", suggesting either the \"test\" agent was abandoned or this was a parallel exploration. Most recently, user has shifted entirely to a travel planning task: a 7-day Tokyo family itinerary with extensive constraints (3 daily activities max, meal requirements, 2+ rainy day alternatives, minimal transfers, fatigue management for a 6-year-old). The assistant executed a 5-phase structured workflow (information gathering → regional clustering → framework → details → final Markdown) and delivered a complete itinerary with specific venue warnings (Ghibli Museum ticket scarcity, teamLab Planets advance booking). User consistently demonstrates preference for: Chinese language communication, structured phased approaches, explicit constraint enumeration, and detailed deliverables with specific formatting requirements.\n\nFacts:\n- [preference | 1.00] User prefers to communicate in 中文 (Chinese)\n- [context | 0.95] User has a 6-year-old child and plans family travel with specific child-centric constraints (fatigue management, activity limits, rainy day contingencies)\n- [behavior | 0.95] User prefers phased, staged work approaches for complex tasks: clarify goals first, collect information, then synthesize — never deliver complete answer immediately\n- [context | 0.90] User is working with a system that supports custom agent creation with SOUL.md configuration files\n- [behavior | 0.90] User provides highly structured requests with numbered constraints and explicit output format specifications (Markdown tables, required sections)\n- [context | 0.90] The \"aaaaaa\" agent design project has been abandoned or indefinitely postponed; user has moved to entirely different task domain (travel planning)\n- [preference | 0.85] User values regional clustering and transfer minimization in travel planning, with specific concern for walking distances and fatigue levels\n</memory>\n\n<current_date>2026-05-11, Monday</current_date>\n</system-reminder>", "additional_kwargs": {"hide_from_ui": true, "dynamic_context_reminder": true}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": null, "id": "6d85432b-5040-4c31-b1d3-06167a98d163"}, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "test"}], "additional_kwargs": {"run_id": "faf2b7dc-f83c-40dd-ae34-c52a21903684", "timestamp": "2026-05-11T11:42:20.906687+00:00"}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": "user-input", "id": "6d85432b-5040-4c31-b1d3-06167a98d163__user"}, {"content": "你好！看到你说 \"test\"——想确认一下，你是想：\n\n1. **继续之前「test」智能体的设计**（简历编辑方向）？\n2. **测试系统是否正常运行**？\n3. **开启一个全新的任务**？\n\n请告诉我你的具体需求，我好继续帮你推进。", "additional_kwargs": {"reasoning_content": "The user simply said \"test\". This could mean several things:\n\n1. Testing if the system/agent is working/responding\n2. Referring back to the \"test\" agent they were working on in the past (resume editing agent)\n3. Just a simple ping/check\n\nGiven the context from memory, the user previously worked on a \"test\" agent for resume editing, then pivoted to \"aaaaaa\", and then to travel planning. Now they've come back to \"test\".\n\nSince this is ambiguous - they might want to continue working on the \"test\" agent, or they might just be testing the connection - I should ask for clarification rather than assuming.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the memory, the user seems to have abandoned the agent projects. The word \"test\" alone is quite ambiguous. I should ask what they want to do. But the instruction says if it's ambiguous, I should ask for clarification.\n\nWait, let me think again. The user's history shows they had a \"test\" agent for resume editing (简历编辑). Then they moved to \"aaaaaa\" which was abandoned, then travel planning. Now they say \"test\" again.\n\nI think the best approach is to acknowledge and ask for clarification about whether they want to continue with the \"test\" agent (resume editing) or if they just want to test the system, or something else.\n\nActually, the user might just be testing if I'm here. A simple response asking what they'd like to do would be appropriate, but given the clarification system rules, if there are multiple valid interpretations, I should ask for clarification.\n\nLet me ask what they mean by \"test\" - whether they want to resume working on the test agent or something else.", "token_usage_attribution": {"version": 1, "kind": "final_answer", "shared_attribution": false, "tool_call_ids": [], "actions": []}}, "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "stop", "model_name": "kimi-k2.6", "system_fingerprint": "fpv0_efa43628", "model_provider": "deepseek"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019e16d8-6651-78f0-8b9e-5eec6723ea65", "tool_calls": [], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 8497, "output_tokens": 411, "total_tokens": 8908, "input_token_details": {}, "output_token_details": {}}}, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "你先在的工作目录是什么"}], "additional_kwargs": {"run_id": "14f18fd4-dfdb-4c39-a32a-7cbe34d76fd7", "timestamp": "2026-05-11T11:43:12.565682+00:00"}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": "user-input", "id": "51b9c186-7f34-4aa2-9db4-16aedd73f07c"}, {"content": "", "additional_kwargs": {"reasoning_content": "用户问的是\"你现在的工作目录是什么\"（或\"你先在的工作目录是什么\"——可能是打字错误，应该是\"现在\"）。\n\n我需要查看当前工作目录的内容来回答这个问题。让我列出 /mnt/user-data/workspace 目录的内容。", "token_usage_attribution": {"version": 1, "kind": "tool_batch", "shared_attribution": false, "tool_call_ids": ["ls:0"], "actions": [{"kind": "tool", "tool_name": "ls", "description": "查看当前工作目录内容", "tool_call_id": "ls:0"}]}}, "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "model_name": "kimi-k2.6", "system_fingerprint": "fpv0_efa43628", "model_provider": "deepseek"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019e16d9-2efd-72d0-860d-d5b7d74072df", "tool_calls": [{"name": "ls", "args": {"description": "查看当前工作目录内容", "path": "/mnt/user-data/workspace"}, "id": "ls:0", "type": "tool_call"}], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 8574, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 8654, "input_token_details": {"cache_read": 8448}, "output_token_details": {}}}, {"content": "(empty)", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "tool", "name": "ls", "id": "010364b8-979e-46a7-a9e5-964da688035f", "tool_call_id": "ls:0", "artifact": null, "status": "success"}, {"content": "我当前的工作目录是 **`/mnt/user-data/workspace`**，目前目录是空的。\n\n这个路径是用于临时文件处理和代码编辑的默认工作区。如果你要上传文件或需要我创建临时文件，都会在这里进行。有什么我可以帮你的吗？", "additional_kwargs": {"reasoning_content": "用户问的是工作目录，我需要告诉他们当前工作目录是 `/mnt/user-data/workspace`，目前是空的。这是一个简单的信息性问题，不需要复杂的推理。", "token_usage_attribution": {"version": 1, "kind": "final_answer", "shared_attribution": false, "tool_call_ids": [], "actions": []}}, "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "stop", "model_name": "kimi-k2.6", "system_fingerprint": "fpv0_efa43628", "model_provider": "deepseek"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019e16d9-4cf6-7882-aa79-33336437d8b9", "tool_calls": [], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 8673, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 8759, "input_token_details": {"cache_read": 8448}, "output_token_details": {}}}, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "在这个目录下帮我用git clone deer-flow 项目"}], "additional_kwargs": {"run_id": "3b066bc3-5b28-4658-89c3-25eaf7e8c604", "timestamp": "2026-05-11T11:44:02.141567+00:00"}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": "user-input", "id": "8482a9b3-32af-4eed-849c-96e8aa131e24"}, {"content": "", "additional_kwargs": {"reasoning_content": "用户要求我在工作目录下用 git clone 拉取 DeerFlow 项目。让我先设置目标，然后执行 clone 操作。\n\nDeerFlow 是 ByteDance 的开源 AI agent 框架，GitHub 地址应该是 https://github.com/bytedance/deer-flow\n\n这是一个相对直接的任务（1步：git clone），不需要 todo list。", "token_usage_attribution": {"version": 1, "kind": "tool_batch", "shared_attribution": false, "tool_call_ids": ["set_objective:1"], "actions": [{"kind": "tool", "tool_name": "set_objective", "description": null, "tool_call_id": "set_objective:1"}]}}, "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "model_name": "kimi-k2.6", "system_fingerprint": "fpv0_efa43628", "model_provider": "deepseek"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019e16d9-f097-7a31-899e-19c7350f1fbe", "tool_calls": [{"name": "set_objective", "args": {"goal": "在 /mnt/user-data/workspace 目录下用 git clone 拉取 DeerFlow 项目", "success_criteria": ["DeerFlow 仓库成功克隆到 /mnt/user-data/workspace/deer-flow 目录"]}, "id": "set_objective:1", "type": "tool_call"}], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 8699, "output_tokens": 138, "total_tokens": 8837, "input_token_details": {"cache_read": 8448}, "output_token_details": {}}}, {"content": "Objective set: 在 /mnt/user-data/workspace 目录下用 git clone 拉取 DeerFlow 项目", "additional_kwargs": {"hide_from_ui": true}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "tool", "name": "set_objective", "id": "e4813f63-705f-4fef-b7c0-14ca25461057", "tool_call_id": "set_objective:1", "artifact": null, "status": "success"}, {"content": "抱歉，我目前没有直接的 Shell / Bash 命令执行权限，无法运行 `git clone` 命令。\n\n如果你需要获取 DeerFlow 项目的代码，我可以提供几个替代方案：\n\n1. **你手动 clone 后上传**：你在本地 `git clone https://github.com/bytedance/deer-flow`，然后将整个目录打包上传，我来帮你分析和处理。\n\n2. **我用其他方式帮你获取**：如果系统支持下载压缩包，我可以尝试下载仓库的 ZIP 文件并解压到工作目录。\n\n3. **系统环境确认**：如果你使用的这个平台本身支持命令行操作（比如某些 agent 环境带有 bash 工具），可能是我这边权限配置的问题。\n\n你希望用哪种方式继续？或者你也可以直接上传 DeerFlow 的相关文件，我可以在这个工作目录里帮你处理。", "additional_kwargs": {"reasoning_content": "用户要求我在工作目录下克隆 DeerFlow 项目。我需要使用 git clone 命令。但我没有直接的命令执行工具。不过，我可以使用 write_file 来写一个脚本，然后... 等等，我没有 bash/shell 执行工具。\n\n让我看看我有什么工具：ls, read_file, write_file, str_replace, web_search, present_files, view_image, ask_clarification, set_objective, report_progress, write_todos。\n\n我没有直接的 shell 执行工具。但这是一个常见任务，我应该尝试用 write_file 写一个 bash 脚本... 不对，我无法执行它。\n\n等等，让我重新检查。实际上，在之前的对话中，我可以使用 read_file 来读取文件，但确实没有看到类似 `bash` 或 `execute` 的工具。\n\n不过，用户明确要求 git clone。我应该诚实地说明我没有 shell 执行权限，或者尝试其他方式。\n\n但实际上，让我再仔细看看... 工具列表里没有 bash/shell 执行工具。我无法直接运行 git clone 命令。\n\n我需要向用户说明这一点，并询问是否有其他方式可以协助，或者提供替代方案（如下载压缩包等）。\n\n等等，让我再想想。也许我可以通过某种方式间接执行？不，我确实没有 shell 工具。\n\n我应该诚实地告诉用户，我没有命令行执行权限，无法直接运行 git clone。", "token_usage_attribution": {"version": 1, "kind": "final_answer", "shared_attribution": false, "tool_call_ids": [], "actions": []}}, "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "stop", "model_name": "kimi-k2.6", "system_fingerprint": "fpv0_efa43628", "model_provider": "deepseek"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019e16da-16e4-7f13-bc95-9a68af6b9bea", "tool_calls": [], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 8878, "output_tokens": 436, "total_tokens": 9314, "input_token_details": {"cache_read": 8448}, "output_token_details": {}}}, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "我已经打开了权限 你再试着 clone 一下"}], "additional_kwargs": {"run_id": "8c1c0e6f-c5d7-4fe4-8288-d2cc81ccfa74", "timestamp": "2026-05-11T13:55:49.856199+00:00"}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "human", "name": "user-input", "id": "56278659-47bf-42ca-a53e-f535972b7800"}, {"content": "", "additional_kwargs": {"reasoning_content": "用户说已经打开了权限，让我再试一次。我现在可以用 bash 工具执行命令了。让我直接运行 git clone 来拉取 DeerFlow 项目。", "token_usage_attribution": {"version": 1, "kind": "tool_batch", "shared_attribution": false, "tool_call_ids": ["bash:2"], "actions": [{"kind": "tool", "tool_name": "bash", "description": "在工作目录下 git clone DeerFlow 项目", "tool_call_id": "bash:2"}]}}, "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "model_name": "kimi-k2.6", "system_fingerprint": "fpv0_8cab9aba", "model_provider": "deepseek"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019e1752-9a19-7d72-a455-c75eb5a0e8d8", "tool_calls": [{"name": "bash", "args": {"description": "在工作目录下 git clone DeerFlow 项目", "command": "cd /mnt/user-data/workspace && git clone https://github.com/bytedance/deer-flow.git"}, "id": "bash:2", "type": "tool_call"}], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 9100, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 9185, "input_token_details": {"cache_read": 512}, "output_token_details": {}}}, {"content": "Cloning into 'deer-flow'...\n", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}, "type": "tool", "name": "bash", "id": "338ca27b-4b1f-4f98-9f1e-b48fdba71cbe", "tool_call_id": "bash:2", "artifact": null, "status": "success"}, {"content": "", "additional_kwargs": {"reasoning_content": "用户已经成功运行了 git clone 命令，输出显示 \"Cloning into 'deer-flow'...\"，这是正常进展中的输出。让我等待克隆完成，但我已经收到了输出。让我确认一下克隆是否成功，看看目录内容。", "token_usage_attribution": {"version": 1, "kind": "tool_batch", "shared_attribution": false, "tool_call_ids": ["ls:3"], "actions": [{"kind": "tool", "tool_name": "ls", "description": "确认 DeerFlow 项目克隆结果", "tool_call_id": "ls:3"}]}}, "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "model_name": "kimi-k2.6", "system_fingerprint": "fpv0_8cab9aba", "model_provider": "deepseek"}, "type": "ai", "name": null, "id": "lc_run--019e1752-cf4a-72c3-85bc-9ca880ef31e3", "tool_calls": [{"name": "ls", "args": {"description": "确认 DeerFlow 项目克隆结果", "path": "/mnt/user-data/workspace/deer-flow"}, "id": "ls:3", "type": "tool_call"}], "invalid_tool_calls": [], "usage_metadata": {"input_tokens": 9210, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 9294, "input_token_details": {"cache_read": 8960}, "output_token_details": {}}}